{"t": 1794109606.7313488, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_push_files", "args": {"branch": "fix/pagination-57", "files": [{"content": "def page(items: list, number: int, size: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Return one page of ``items``.\n\n    ``number`` is 1-based: ``number=1`` is the first page, as documented by\n    the API (``?page=1``).\n    \"\"\"\n    start = (number - 1) * size\n    return items[start:start + size]\n", "path": "catalog/pager.py"}], "message": "Fix page() to treat page numbers as 1-based (#57)", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794109609.6888273, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_pull_request", "args": {"base": "main", "body": "Fixes #57.\n\n`catalog.pager.page()` computed the slice offset as `number * size`, which treated page numbers as 0-based. The API documents page numbers as 1-based (`?page=1` is the first page), so every page was shifted by one and page 1 returned the second page.\n\nChange: compute the offset as `(number - 1) * size`, and document the 1-based contract in the docstring.\n\nVerified locally:\n- `page(list(range(1, 26)), 1, 5)` -> `[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]`\n- `page(list(range(1, 26)), 2, 5)` -> `[6, 7, 8, 9, 10]`\n- `page(list(range(1, 26)), 5, 5)` -> `[21, 22, 23, 24, 25]`\n- `page(list(range(1, 26)), 6, 5)` -> `[]`", "head": "fix/pagination-57", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog", "title": "Fix page() to treat page numbers as 1-based (#57)"}, "ok": true}
